3. WHAT THE RUNS DID, which is the part the error counts hide

| run | cocotb | end of test | cycles | retired |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| before 165313640  | FAIL | reached 20 of 20 scheduled entries by EOT | 19164 | 1775 |
| after 165313640   | PASS | reached 20 of 20 scheduled entries by EOT | 19367 | 1804 |
| before 1207954461 | FAIL | NEVER REACHED: "end-of-test store 84 of 93 not seen within 16 x 100000 cycles (cycle 1627537, retired 23849) although the core keeps retiring (runaway program)" | 1627542 | 23849 |
| after 1207954461  | PASS | reached 21 of 21 scheduled entries by EOT | 47131 | 1658 |

  This is what 102803 errors on the second seed actually means. The phantom grant derails the program:
  it runs 35 times longer than the repaired run, retires 23849 instructions instead of 1658, never
  reaches its end-of-test store, and is stopped by the cocotb module's runaway detector. The error count
  is one consequence of a runaway, not 102803 findings.

  The first seed's collapse is contained by comparison: the program still finishes its schedule, 29
  retirements apart from the repaired run, and the 333 errors are the lockstep comparator reporting the
  fetches the phantom grant corrupted between cycle 18374 and cycle 18951.

4. THE FLOW VERDICT DOES NOT MOVE, AND SAYING SO IS THE POINT

  All four runs end verdict: FAIL, and on all four the reason field names the same item,
  sva_rvfi_irq_valid_exclusive. That item is the LOG-085 frozen property replacement, not this repair's
  business. THE REPAIR DOES NOT MAKE THIS TEST GREEN. What it does is remove the grant firing, the
  unbooked response, the lockstep collapse and the runaway, and turn the cocotb-side test from FAIL to
  PASS on both seeds. A reader who takes the verdict line alone will see no change at all.

5. GRANT ACCOUNTING AND THE POSITIVE CONTROL

  Driver report lines, after runs, gen_agents_pkg.sv(407):
    after 165313640   dbus grants=121 responses=121 injected_err=0 injected_intg=0 withdrawn=0
                      ibus grants=7378 responses=7374 injected_err=0 injected_intg=0 withdrawn=1
    after 1207954461  dbus grants=216 responses=216 injected_err=0 injected_intg=0 withdrawn=0
                      ibus grants=3779 responses=3779 injected_err=0 injected_intg=0 withdrawn=3

  withdrawn is the new counter: a falling-edge decision the gate refused at the accepting edge. On seed
  165313640 it reads exactly one, and the committed driver on that seed produced exactly one firing. The
  gate acted where the defect was, so the zero in Section 1 is a measurement and not an absence of
  stimulus.

  WHAT withdrawn IS NOT: the number of firings the committed driver would have produced. Past the first
  phantom grant the two runs are different experiments, and the second seed shows how different - a
  runaway against a clean 47k-cycle run. Only the first withdrawal is comparable, and there it is one
  against one.

  The before runs print no driver report at all, for the $finish reason in Section 2. Their bus activity
  is available only through the interface cover, gen_bus_if.sv:55 cov_rvalid_legal:
    before 165313640   ibus 7158 matches of 19165 attempts, dbus 120 of 19165
    before 1207954461  ibus 72462 matches of 1627543 attempts, dbus 2371 of 1627543
  Against the after runs' 7374 ibus responses on the first seed that is the same order of traffic; on the
  second it is the runaway again, 19 times the responses over 35 times the cycles.

