  nothing on the data side was relying on a grant standing over a withdrawn request.

7. A DIFFERENCE FROM THE PAIR RECORD I AM NOT RESOLVING HERE

  rtl-arch's pair record also lists, for seed 165313640, sva_ibus_rvalid_outstanding 8 firings and
  sva_ibus_outstanding_max 280. My before run on this base reads 1 and none. The pair record's runs come
  from the wave regression under /proj_soc/user_dev/fzhang/ibex_dv_out/regress_wave_4017573, a base
  older than the saturating-counter landings, and those two ids are precisely the every-cycle floods
  that a wrapping outstanding counter produced and that those landings removed. That is the explanation
  the numbers fit; I have not rebuilt their base to confirm it, so it stands as a reading and not a
  measurement. It does not touch this repair either way: the grant firing itself reproduces at the tick.
